SUMMARY:Galileo
LOCATION:Shubert Theatre, 225 West 44th Street, New York NY 10036
DESCRIPTION:<p><em>&nbsp;Galileo</em>&nbsp;is the electrifying and
  explosive new Broadway musical about the man whose discoveries rocked our
  universe.<br /><br />When luminary Galileo (four-time Tony Award&reg;
  nominee Ra&uacute;l Esparza) peers into the heavens, what he sees
  challenges humanity&rsquo;s understanding of the world. Unwilling to deny
  the truth, Galileo finds himself in a fight with the most powerful
  institution on Earth. As his trusted confidant Barberini (Drama Desk Award
  nominee Jeremy Kushnier) ascends to power, friendship leads to betrayal,
  and the dreams Galileo has envisioned for himself and for his brilliant
  daughter Virginia (Tony&reg; nominee Joy Woods) begin to slip away.
  Belief, ambition, and love pull the trio out of orbit, each confronting
  what they&rsquo;re willing to sacrifice for what matters most.<br /><br
  /><em>Galileo</em> tells the story of the man whose wonder and curiosity
  changed the world. Featuring a star-studded creative team, with a book by
  Danny Strong (<em>Dopesick</em>, <em>Empire</em>) and an original score by
  Zoe Sarnak (<em>The Lonely Few</em>, <em>Empire Records</em>) and Michael
  Weiner (<em>13 Going on 30</em>, <em>First Date</em>), <em>Galileo</em> is
  directed by Tony&reg; winner Michael Mayer (<em>American Idiot</em>,
  <em>Spring Awakening</em>) and choreographed by Tony&reg; nominee David
  Neumann (<em>Hadestown</em>, <em>Swept Away</em>).</p>
END:VEVENT
